:99999},{"input":[{"__gen__":"sorted","n":100000,"lo":-1000000,"hi":1000000,"seed":1009,"unique":true,"step":5},28152],"output":50000},{"input":[{"__gen__":"sorted","n":100000,"lo":-1000000,"hi":1000000,"seed":1009,"unique":true,"step":5},1007355],"output":-1}],"hints":["Keep a half-open window `[lo, hi)` and shrink it by half each step. Watch the loop condition."],"complexity":"O(log n) time, O(1) space","starter":{"python":"def search(nums, target):\n    # TODO: implement\n    pass\n","javascript":"/**\n * @param {*} nums\n * @param {*} target\n * @return {*}\n */\nvar search = function (nums, target) {\n  // TODO: implement\n};\n"},"editorial":{"explanation":"Keep a window `[lo, hi]` that is the only place the target could still be. Compare with the middle\nelement: if it is smaller, the answer is to the right, so move `lo`; if larger, move `hi`.\n\nEvery comparison halves the window, so it finishes in `O(log n)` with `O(1)` space.\n\nTwo details bite people: use `lo + (hi - lo) // 2` in languages where `lo + hi` can overflow, and\nbe consistent about whether `hi` is inclusive — mixing the two conventions is how off-by-one\ninfinite loops happen.","code":{"python":"def search(nums, target):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(nums) - 1\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if nums[mid] == target:\n            return mid\n        if nums[mid] < target:\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    return -1\n"},"complexity":"O(log n) time, O(1) space"}}
